input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, which didn't match its own docstring.\n\n**Change:** `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` when quantizing to cents.\n\n- `2.675 -> 2.68` (unchanged)\n- `2.665 -> 2.66` (was 2.67)\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNote: amounts that land exactly on a half-cent where the cent digit is even will now round down instead of up. This is the intended FIN-212 behavior.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the PR may or may not have been created. I'll check before retrying so I don't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019BUotbNmVvMGH6gmSKzv8D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 was created despite the timeout, but alex isn't on it as a reviewer yet. Adding him now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QoptthBwsgSMyBzVV6o74C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why the test failed: `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`. No other files changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on the fix.\n- **PR #101:** The request to open it timed out. I checked before retrying, and the PR had been created but without a reviewer, so I added alex rather than opening a second one.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\n**Behavior change:** amounts that fall exactly on a half-cent now round to the nearest even cent. For example, `2.665` now rounds down to `2.66`. This is what FIN-212 asks for, but anything that relied on the old round-half-up results will see slightly different numbers.", "type": "text"}]}]}